---
import AppLayout from '../../../../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import { uploadfit, appPath, studio, supportLink } from '../../../../data/apps';

const sections = [
  ['images', 'Images, files and device access'],
  ['advertising', 'Rewarded ads and Google AdMob'],
  ['purchases', 'Pro purchases and RevenueCat'],
  ['support', 'Support messages'],
  ['sharing', 'How information is used and shared'],
  ['choices', 'Your choices and privacy rights'],
  ['retention', 'Retention and deletion'],
  ['security', 'Security and international processing'],
  ['children', 'Children’s privacy'],
  ['changes', 'Changes and contact'],
];
---

<AppLayout
  title="UploadFit Privacy Policy | AppCrazy Labs"
  description="UploadFit’s privacy policy: on-device image processing, AdMob rewarded ads, RevenueCat purchases, data retention, deletion and privacy contact details."
  canonicalPath={`${appPath(uploadfit)}privacy/`}
  heading="UploadFit privacy policy"
  kicker="AppCrazy Labs · Privacy"
  backLabel="UploadFit"
  backHref={appPath(uploadfit)}
>
  <div slot="meta" class="note-meta">
    <span>Effective: <time datetime="2026-10-03">3 October 2026</time></span>
    <span>Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-03">3 October 2026</time></span>
  </div>

  <p class="archive-disclaimer">
    <strong>Legal developer / publisher:</strong> [To be confirmed: exact developer name shown in Google Play Console].
    <br />
    <strong>Privacy contact:</strong> Sidhanshu Udawat, AppCrazy Labs.
  </p>
  <p>
    This policy explains how UploadFit, an image utility offered under the AppCrazy Labs
    studio brand, handles information when you use the app or contact support.
    In this policy, “we”, “us” and “our” refer to the developer of UploadFit.
    For privacy enquiries, contact{' '}
    <a href={supportLink('UploadFit privacy enquiry')}>{studio.email}</a>.
  </p>
  <aside class="note-callout" aria-label="Privacy summary">
    <strong>The essentials</strong>
    <p>
      Your images are processed on your device and are not uploaded to our servers.
      No UploadFit account is required. AdMob handles advertising data, and RevenueCat
      handles purchase and entitlement information. Neither service processes your images.
    </p>
  </aside>
  <p>
    UploadFit currently integrates AdMob and RevenueCat. It does not use a separate
    analytics or crash-reporting SDK. This does not mean that no data leaves the device:
    the advertising and purchase services described below have their own data processing.
  </p>

  <nav class="policy-contents" aria-label="Privacy policy contents">
    <strong>In this policy</strong>
    <ol>{sections.map(([id, label]) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{label}</a></li>)}</ol>
  </nav>

  <section id="images" aria-labelledby="images-title">
    <h2 id="images-title">1. Images, files and device access</h2>
    <p>
      UploadFit accesses the images you select to resize, crop, compress, convert,
      preview and save or share them. These operations take place locally on your device.
      We do not receive or store those images on our servers, and do not send them to
      AdMob or RevenueCat.
    </p>
    <p>
      The app uses your device’s file selection and storage facilities to open images
      and save results. Where your operating system requires permission for this access,
      you control it through its permission prompts and settings.
      If you choose to share a result, the receiving app or service receives that image
      and its own privacy policy applies. Device or gallery backups are also governed
      by your device settings and backup provider.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="advertising" aria-labelledby="advertising-title">
    <h2 id="advertising-title">2. Rewarded ads and Google AdMob</h2>
    <p>
      UploadFit offers rewarded ads through Google AdMob. Google’s Mobile Ads SDK
      collects and shares information such as IP addresses, device or advertising
      identifiers, ad and app interactions, and diagnostic information. An IP address
      may be used to estimate a general location. Processing depends on SDK settings,
      device settings, consent and the ad served.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google and its advertising partners use this information to deliver and measure
      advertising, prevent fraud and maintain their services. Where permitted and
      consented to, it can also support personalised advertising. Non-personalised ads
      can still involve data processing for delivery, measurement and fraud prevention.
      Image contents are not part of this advertising data.
    </p>
    <p>
      Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s Privacy Policy</a> and{' '}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from apps that use its services</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="purchases" aria-labelledby="purchases-title">
    <h2 id="purchases-title">3. Pro purchases and RevenueCat</h2>
    <p>
      UploadFit offers an optional one-time lifetime Pro purchase. Google Play processes
      the payment. RevenueCat helps validate purchases and manage access to Pro features,
      including restoration of eligible purchases.
    </p>
    <p>
      RevenueCat processes purchase history, product and transaction identifiers,
      purchase tokens or receipts, purchase status and entitlement information. It uses
      an app user identifier, which can be generated without you creating an account.
      Technical context such as the app version, platform, locale and currency may
      accompany these requests.
    </p>
    <p>
      This information supports purchase validation, entitlement management, support,
      fraud prevention and purchase reporting. RevenueCat does not receive your images.
      We and RevenueCat do not receive your full payment card details from Google Play.{' '}
      See <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy">RevenueCat’s Privacy Policy</a> and{' '}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s Privacy Policy</a> for their practices.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="support" aria-labelledby="support-title">
    <h2 id="support-title">4. Support messages</h2>
    <p>
      If you email us, we receive your email address, the content of your message and
      any attachments you choose to send. We use this information to respond, investigate
      problems and handle privacy or purchase requests. Our email provider processes
      these messages to deliver and store them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Please do not send sensitive images or payment card details. Sending an image
      voluntarily to support is separate from the app’s local image processing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="sharing" aria-labelledby="sharing-title">
    <h2 id="sharing-title">5. How information is used and shared</h2>
    <p>
      We use information to provide the features you request, manage purchases,
      respond to support, protect against misuse and meet legal obligations.
      Recipients include Google for advertising and payments, RevenueCat for purchase
      management, and our email provider for support. We may also disclose information
      when legally required or necessary to protect users’ rights and safety.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not sell your images or support messages. AdMob’s advertising-related
      sharing is described above. Where data protection law requires a legal basis,
      processing relies on providing requested services, legitimate interests such as
      security and support, legal obligations, or consent where required for advertising
      and device identifiers.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="choices" aria-labelledby="choices-title">
    <h2 id="choices-title">6. Your choices and privacy rights</h2>
    <p>
      You choose which images to open, what to save or share, and whether to make a Pro
      purchase. You can manage file permissions and advertising identifier settings
      through Android, with available controls depending on your device and version.
      Use any advertising consent or privacy controls presented in the app to express
      or update your preferences. Where consent is required, you may withdraw it.
      Contact us if you need help with these choices.
    </p>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete or
      obtain a copy of personal information, restrict or object to processing, and
      withdraw consent. You may also complain to your local data protection authority.
      Email <a href={supportLink('UploadFit privacy request')}>{studio.email}</a> to
      exercise these rights. We may need limited information to verify the request
      and locate the relevant record. We cannot access images stored only on your device.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="retention" aria-labelledby="retention-title">
    <h2 id="retention-title">7. Retention and deletion</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Images and local app data:</strong> we retain no server copies of images
        processed in the app. Delete exported files using your gallery or file manager.
        Android’s clear-storage or uninstall controls remove app-managed local data;
        exported images and backups may remain until you delete them separately.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Purchase records:</strong> purchase and entitlement records are retained
        as needed to provide and restore Pro access, resolve disputes, prevent fraud and
        meet applicable legal requirements. Uninstalling UploadFit does not automatically
        delete RevenueCat or Google Play records.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Advertising data:</strong> Google and its partners retain advertising data
        under their own retention policies and the controls they provide.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Support messages:</strong> we keep correspondence only for as long as
        needed to resolve the request and follow-up issues, or to meet legal obligations,
        after which it is deleted.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To request deletion of support messages or purchase records we manage through
      RevenueCat, email <a href={supportLink('UploadFit data deletion request')}>{studio.email}</a>{' '}
      with the subject “UploadFit data deletion request”. We will explain any information
      needed to locate your record and any retention required by law. Deleting purchase
      records may affect our ability to recognise or restore Pro access; it does not
      itself issue a refund or erase Google Play’s transaction records. Continued use
      or a purchase restore may create a new RevenueCat record.
    </p>
    <p>No UploadFit account is required, so there is no UploadFit account to close.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="security" aria-labelledby="security-title">
    <h2 id="security-title">8. Security and international processing</h2>
    <p>
      Keeping image processing on your device limits exposure of image contents.
      AdMob and RevenueCat use encrypted connections for data sent to their services.
      We limit access to support and purchase information to handling the purposes
      described in this policy. No storage or transmission method can guarantee
      absolute security.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google, RevenueCat and our email provider may process information in countries
      other than your own, including the United States. Their privacy policies describe
      the safeguards used for international transfers. This does not change where
      UploadFit processes your images: image operations remain on your device.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="children" aria-labelledby="children-title">
    <h2 id="children-title">9. Children’s privacy</h2>
    <p>
      UploadFit is a general-purpose image utility and is not specifically directed at
      children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children
      under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal information to us, contact
      us so we can investigate and arrange appropriate deletion.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes" aria-labelledby="changes-title">
    <h2 id="changes-title">10. Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy as UploadFit or its service providers change. The latest
      version will be published on this page with a revised date. Where required, we
      will provide additional notice or request consent for material changes.
    </p>
    <p>
      For UploadFit privacy questions, support or deletion requests, email{' '}
      <a href={supportLink('UploadFit privacy enquiry')}>{studio.email}</a>.
      You can also use the <a href="/#contact">existing website contact links</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</AppLayout>
